<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">A single asset registry that stays current and benefits all. <span>Operational excellence starts with three checks.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <div class="split split--top">
      <div>
        <ul class="feature-runs feature-runs--stack">
          <li><h3>The whole company keeps it current</h3><p>Crowdsourced from every crew, planner, and permit holder: each inspection, work order, and environmental permit writes back to the asset record.</p></li>
          <li><h3>The record matches the field</h3><p>Type, current location, parent/child/flow associations, and spec data, with user-defined attributes for each equipment type.</p></li>
          <li><h3>The record holds up to an audit</h3><p>An immutable change log shows who changed what, and when. Emission sources are assets too, so environmental permits and inspections improve the same record.</p></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="top-card">
          <div class="top-card-panel">
            <ul class="tags tags--white">
              <li>ISO 55000 • Asset Management</li>
              <li>ISO 14224 • Maintenance and Reliability</li>
              <li>API 653 • Storage Tanks</li>
              <li>ISO 50001 • Energy Management</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">PHMSA 49 CFR 192/195 • Pipelines</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">EPA 40 CFR 60 • NSPS</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">EPA 40 CFR 80 • Fuels &amp; Fuel Additives</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">EPA 40 CFR 98 • GHG Reporting</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">EPA 40 CFR 112 • SPCC</li>
              <li class="is-regulation">EU 2024/1787 • Methane Regulation</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p>Configure to global standards; adaptable to your needs.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head section-head--run">
      <h2 class="headline-run">One record, three uses. <span>Operations, engineering, and environmental teams work from the same asset record, so nothing has to be reconciled by hand later.</span></h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="bento">
      <li class="bento-card">
        <img class="bento-card-media" src="/static/img/assets/condition.webp" width="386" height="193" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <h3 class="h4">Asset tracking &amp; O&amp;M</h3>
        <p>Location, condition, and criticality on every asset. Condition scores update from inspections, sensor data, and maintenance history, and set inspection frequency and work priority.</p>
        <a class="text-action" href="/workflows">See Workflow Automation</a>
      </li>
      <li class="bento-card">
        <img class="bento-card-media" src="/static/img/assets/registry.webp" width="386" height="193" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <h3 class="h4">Facility engineering</h3>
        <p>Hierarchy, spec data, drawings, and documents in one structured record. Bulk-import from your CMMS or ERP, or build it directly.</p>
        <a class="text-action" href="/assets/operations">See the data foundation</a>
      </li>
      <li class="bento-card">
        <img class="bento-card-media" src="/static/img/assets/criticality.webp" width="386" height="193" alt="" loading="lazy">
        <h3 class="h4">Emissions</h3>
        <p>Fuel use and run hours feed calculation groups for the GHG and state inventories as data arrives.</p>
        <a class="text-action" href="/platform/emissions">See emissions reporting</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

